Subject: Plug-in: specialisations matched by the bytes that decide them; the alignment answers behind a switch, off

A pipeline of the generic uber shader kept up to 64 contents of its deciding
buffer, each matched by all its bytes and never dropped. The garbage after the
structure's last field made every arrival of a configuration a new content: a
slot, a compilation in the background -- and once the slots were full, the
unspecialised program (32064 instruction words) for everything new until the
window server restarted. A slot now keeps the bytes its program's compilation
read (hakios_metal_program_known_reads), and a content that agrees with it in
those is that slot; 128 slots, and a line in the console if they ever fill.
metal_spec_mask=0 matches by all the bytes again.

The alignment answers of e22b881 are behind metal_align, and off: with all of
them at 64 CoreAnimation takes nearly every image as client storage
(-newBufferWithBytesNoCopy: and a texture over the buffer, labelled
com.apple.coreanimation.image-client-storage in the frame traces) where it
uploaded most of them, and a no-copy buffer here is a copy made when the buffer
is made: the widgets whose bitmaps arrive later -- the Calendar, the headlines
-- were drawn from the empty copy, invisible. Bit 1 answers the IOSurface pair,
bit 2 the linear four; which of them brings client storage on is not
established, and neither belongs on by default until a no-copy buffer shares
the caller's memory. The first queue prints the answers in force.

metal_swizzle=0 leaves a descriptor's swizzle unapplied, for a bisect.


